82:/// Interface size (File › Options › General, `ui.interfaceSize`): how large the ribbon, menus, panes
83:/// and dialogs are drawn, through egui's zoom factor. Document zoom (View › Zoom) is a separate
84:/// setting and never changes with it.
85:///
86:/// `Auto` (the default) keeps the display scale the system reports. A chosen size is absolute, as in
87:/// PhotoCraft and PdfCraft (#822): "100%" is one screen pixel per point whatever the display reports,
88:/// so a system that guesses 200 % (a bare window manager on X11, where winit falls back to the
89:/// monitor's DPI) doesn't make "100%" draw at 200 %. The display's scale is divided back out in
90:/// [`InterfaceSize::zoom_factor`].
